# ==============================================================================
# J.A.R.V.I.S. 2.0 — ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE (.env.example)
# ==============================================================================
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to '.env':
#      Windows PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#      Linux / macOS:       cp .env.example .env
# 2. Populate at minimum your GEMINI_API_KEY (the only required key).
# 3. All other keys are optional or obsolete with graceful fallbacks.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. CORE COGNITIVE ENGINE (REQUIRED)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Powers 90% of J.A.R.V.I.S. intelligence:
# - Primary conversational reasoning across 4 multi-turn models:
#   * gemini-3.5-flash-lite (primary fast router)
#   * gemini-flash-latest   (adaptive fallback)
#   * gemini-3.8-flash      (deep reasoning)
#   * gemini-2.5-flash      (high-throughput fallback)
# - Native optical vision analysis for desktop screens and camera streams
# - High-dimensional vector embeddings for semantic memory (gemini-embedding-001)
# - Google Antigravity Agent bridge and autonomous reflection engine
# Get a free key at: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. FAST INFERENCE COGNITION (OPTIONAL / CO-PRIMARY FALLBACK)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# High-speed conversational LLM fallback via Groq Cloud (openai/gpt-oss-120b).
# If omitted, J.A.R.V.I.S. automatically routes 100% of reasoning to Gemini.
# Get a free key at: https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key_here

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. SITUATION ROOM NEWS INTELLIGENCE (OPTIONAL)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used exclusively by the standalone tactical news application (apps/news_intel.py)
# for structured multi-category geopolitical and conflict searches.
# NOTE: The main HUD Tactical News widget (services/news_service.py) uses Google News
# RSS feeds and requires NO API KEY.
# If omitted in apps/news_intel.py: Uses local JSON cache (news_matrix_cache.json).
# Get a key at: https://worldnewsapi.com/ (Free tier: 50 requests/day)
WORLDNEWS_API_KEY=your_worldnews_api_key_here
# Alternative alias recognized by apps/news_intel.py:
# NEWS_API_KEY=your_news_api_key_here

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. OPTICAL VISION ARRAY FALLBACK (OPTIONAL)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secondary vision analysis endpoint via OpenRouter (google/gemini-2.0-flash-001).
# If omitted, J.A.R.V.I.S. uses native Gemini vision via GEMINI_API_KEY.
# Get a key at: https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_api_key_here

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. GEOSPATIAL RECON & TACTICAL VECTOR MAPS (NO API KEY REQUIRED)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The J.A.R.V.I.S. 2.0 map subsystem (gui/intel_widgets.py, apps/map_intel.py,
# assets/map_view.html, services/map_service.py) operates on 100% FREE, open-source
# and keyless providers:
# - CartoDB Dark Matter Tiles:      https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/ (Free, no key)
# - Google Satellite & Vector:      https://mt1.google.com/vt/ (Free direct tiles, dark CSS inverted)
# - Nominatim OpenStreetMap Search: https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/ (Free, no key)
# - Esri ArcGIS World Geocoding:    https://geocode.arcgis.com/ (Free public tier, no key)
# - OSRM Driving Route Engine:      http://router.project-osrm.org/ (Free, no key)
#
# NO API KEY IS NEEDED FOR THE CURRENT MAP IMPLEMENTATION.
# (If you choose to integrate commercial vector tile platforms in future custom builds):
# MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_mapbox_token_here   # https://www.mapbox.com/ (Optional)
# MAPTILER_API_KEY=your_maptiler_key_here     # https://www.maptiler.com/ (Optional)

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. OBSOLETE & RESERVED KEYS (OPTIONAL / UNUSED)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The following keys are either legacy placeholders or reserved for future extensions.
# All active systems run cleanly without them.

# Weather Services (OBSOLETE): J.A.R.V.I.S. migrated entirely to Open-Meteo
# (https://open-meteo.com/), which is 100% free and requires NO API KEY.
WEATHER_API_KEY=
ACCUWEATHER_API_KEY=

# Reserved LLM Providers (UNUSED in active runtime; safe to leave blank):
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
SAMBANOVA_API_KEY=
GITHUB_API_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. HARDWARE IOT & GOOGLE WORKSPACE NOTES (NON-ENV CREDENTIALS)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Smart Home Lighting (Havells / Tuya Bulb):
#   - Controlled locally over LAN via 'tinytuya' library.
#   - Credentials reside in 'tinytuya.json' (apiKey, apiSecret, apiDeviceID)
#     and hardcoded LAN defaults in 'core/iot.py' (DEVICE_ID, IP_ADDRESS, LOCAL_KEY).
#   - If bulb is offline or unreachable, system logs a silent hardware notice and continues.
#
# Google Workspace Suite (Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Tasks):
#   - Authenticates via OAuth 2.0 Desktop Application tokens.
#   - Credentials reside in 'credentials.json' (client secret) and 'token.json' (user session).
#   - If missing or expired, system logs "Workspace offline" and runs all core systems normally.
# ==============================================================================
